# Every rule here is ANCHORED with a leading slash.
#
# Before this rewrite none of them were, so each pattern matched at any depth.
# Two consequences, both real:
#   - `00-Session-Brief.md` stayed invisible to git after it was moved into
#     claude-logs/, which is why 23 references pointed at a file that a clone
#     did not contain — while six document headers called it the binding source.
#   - `Check-In-Presentation*07.09` will stop matching once that folder is
#     renamed. One `git add -A` at the wrong moment would then commit 42 MB of
#     .pptx and .mp4 permanently into history. Both the old and the new path are
#     listed below so no window exists where that folder is unignored.

# --- Local tooling ------------------------------------------------------------
/.claude/

# --- Coursework binaries: slides, video, and Office lock files ----------------
# 42 MB, needed for the school submission, useless to an implementer.
/Check-In-Presentation 07.09/
/coursework/check-in-presentation-2026-09-07/
~$*

# --- Deliberately NOT ignored anymore ----------------------------------------
# `00-Session-Brief.md` and `Initial-Claude-Prompt.md` are now tracked. The
# brief is the decision protocol the whole chain rests on; shipping specs that
# name a source of truth absent from the repo was the worst defect in the tree.
# See docs/README.md for the precedence order it sits in.
